<%# PREVIEW - create, on the same shape as the record page.

    **max-w-3xl, not max-w-7xl.** Measured at 1366px: this form was 1047px wide, and the record page it
    leads to is 768px, for the same three fields. design.md records that defect on `classrooms#edit` - a
    form's measure does not scale with the window - and every admin create page still has it.

    **One section, Details, with the same heading the record page uses.** A student who does not exist yet
    has no portfolio to pay into and no grade book to have been marked in, so the money and attendance
    sections have nothing to show. The heading matching is the point: a section that is called something
    different on the create page is the inconsistency this shape exists to remove. %>
<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
  <%= admin_breadcrumbs(@breadcrumbs) %>

  <%= render layout: "components/ui/page_header",
             locals: { title: "New student",
                       description: "You can add money and see attendance once the account exists." } do %><% end %>

  <div class="space-y-6">
    <%= render layout: "admin/shared/record_section",
               locals: { title: "Details", hint: "Saved when you press Create student." } do %>
      <%= render "form" %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
